  "task": {
    "objective": "Scouts coordinate local sensors, finite pulses, physical beacons and tags to capture the two player-controlled runners; runners use routes, smoke, jams and exits.",
    "natural_termination": "Both runners resolved as captured or escaped, otherwise horizon seventy-two. Captured and escaped runners are inactive and may only wait. Capture precedes simultaneous escape. Natural completion takes priority at the horizon.",
    "interaction": "A directional pulse shares a live runner track with the other scout. Beacons expose nearby runners even through smoke. Runner smoke cancels pulse tracking, and physical jams defeat simultaneous activation. Tags and escapes change both teams' rewards; finite tokens compete between information actions and dashes.",
    "observation_access": "Fixed map, beacons, exits and aggregate resolved counts are public. Teammates share exact state. Scout zero senses Manhattan one plus a horizontal three-cell beam, scout one Manhattan one plus a vertical three-cell beam. Runners sense Manhattan two. Sensors ignore wall occlusion by explicit radio-rule convention. Pulse tracks and beacon coverage are shared only with scouts. Smoke blocks non-adjacent ordinary scout sensing and cancels pulse tracks; beacons pierce it. Hidden payloads are minus one."
  },
